gxr-key-remap is maintained as a native package because the daemons and their
Ubuntu service integration are released from the same repository.

Launchpad versions must be unique. For subsequent PPA uploads, add a changelog
entry and increment the +gxrN component. The changelog version uses a
~YY.MM.N suffix for its target series; packaging/publish.sh reuses that entry
for every selected series with the matching Ubuntu version suffix.

Publishing uses a Podman image of each selected Ubuntu series, defaulting to
stonking. Use --series resolute to select resolute; --series is repeatable.
The image installs the build dependencies from debian/control and is rebuilt
when that file or packaging/Containerfile changes.

Use ./packaging/publish.sh --no-upload for a signed dry run. Add --test-build
to build arm64 binaries from the extracted source package before uploading.
The build cross-compiles on amd64 and runs natively on arm64. Runtime tests
are skipped when cross-compiling. The host needs Podman, Git, and GnuPG;
--unsigned skips signing and implies --no-upload.

Clean builds archive HEAD, excluding packaging/. To validate local changes,
use --allow-dirty with --no-upload or --unsigned. Source artifacts and any
test-built binary packages are retained in build/publish/.
